        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. US-Israeli strikes destroy Iranian highway bridge Middle East Issued on: 03/04/2026 - 11:47 Modified: 03/04/2026 - 11:57 It is the tallest bridge in the Middle East, according to Iranian media. The B1 bridge only 35km of Tehran was destroyed in two US-Israeli strikes on April 2. Trump threatened energy plants could be next if Iran didn't agree to a deal to end the conflict. ‘Disturbing trend’ of US-Israeli strikes hitting non-military targets in Iran 03/04/2026 Middle East Europe, NATO under pressure over Iran war: 'Trump strong with the weak and weak with the strong' 02/04/2026 Middle East Israel's Lebanon endgame: 'Dismantle Hezbollah entirely as a political and social movement' 02/04/2026 Middle East US and Israel 'again bombing what were clearly non-military sites' in Iran 02/04/2026 Middle East US war on Iran: 'Absolute disaster' for Middle Eastern airlines 02/04/2026 Middle East Trump claims Iran wants a ceasefire, Iran says remarks are ‘false and baseless’ 01/04/2026 Middle East 'Strategy of ecological terror. Desalination as a weapon of war' in the Middle East 01/04/2026 Middle East US journalist Shelly Kittleson kidnapped in Iraq 01/04/2026 Middle East Death penalty 'a deep stain on the law books of the state of Israel' 01/04/2026 Middle East"
